  "description": "HUZMIZ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C98 H71 Cl3 O14 S8 Tb4,4.32(C1 H4 O1),1.58(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb1B (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb2B (Tb) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.555-5.070 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.60-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Tb4(μ4-OH)(PTC4A)2Cl3(CH3OH)2(H2O)3]·4.3CH3OH·1.6H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
